   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the commissioner of general services to transfer and convey\ncertain unappropriated state land to the town of Bedford",
    "basePrintNo": "S8349",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8349-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8349\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act authorizing the commissioner of general\nservices to transfer and convey certain unappropriated state land to the\ntown of Bedford\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAuthorizes the  commissioner of general services to convey an abandoned\nparcel of land to the Town of Bedford for the expansion of a wastewater\ntreatment facility.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one authorizes the commissioner of general services, subject to\nthe consent of the commissioner of corrections and community super-\nvision, to transfer and convey to the Town of Bedford, abandoned state\nland owned by the department of corrections within the Town of Bedford,\nfor the sum of one dollar and upon conditions as the commissioner of\ngeneral services may deem proper.\n\nSection two provides a geographical description of the land to be trans-\nferred and conveyed.\n\nSection three states that the description within section two is not\nintended to be a legal description but intended to identify the parcel\nto be conveyed. And that as a condition of the transfer, the Town of\nBedford may submit to the commissioner of general services an accurate\nsurvey and description of the lands to be conveyed, which may be used in\nthe conveyance thereof.\n\nSection four states that the office of general services shall not trans-\nfer or convey the aforesaid land unless an application is made by the\nTown of Bedford within 1 year after the effective date of this act and\nthat said application shall be in the form of a resolution setting forth\na comprehensive statement approved by its Town Board acknowledging and\naccepting the use restrictions set forth within section five.\n\nSection five establishes that the land shall only be used for the\npurpose of operating a wastewater treatment plant and operations as may\nbe reasonably necessary. If any other purpose is undertaken, it shall\nrevert back to the State of New York.\n\nSection six sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOver the years, the Department of Corrections and Community Supervision\nhas assisted in making surplus property available to municipalities and\nnot-for-profit corporations upon a showing of important need when the\nproperty is no longer needed. In this instance, a waste water treatment\nfacility, located at the Bedford Hills Correctional Facility, is no\nlonger needed by the state and is currently not being used to its maxi-\nmum potential. The Town of Bedford seeks to utilize this facility to its\nmaximum output, thereby increasing wastewater services for the town\nincluding the nearby Business District, residential community and the\nelementary school. It would also increase service to the Bedford Correc-\ntional Facility. The transfer would also allow the town to take advan-\ntage of grants that are unavailable to others to substantially improve\nwater and sewer services. This transfer would also prevent the Town of\nBedford from having to construct its own wastewater facility which would\ncost taxpayers millions of dollars.\n\nThe transfer of land has received statements of approval from the\nDepartment of Corrections and Community Supervision, the New York City\nDepartment of Environmental Protection and the New York State Office of\nGeneral Services.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nVirtually none to the State. Will result in savings for the Town of\nBedford.\n\n \nEFFECTS ON FINES, PENAL SANCTIONS AND OTHER PENALTIES:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nShall take effect immediately\n",
